    "created_at": "2023-09-13T05:52:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-13T05:52:15Z",
    "body": "It would be good to write tests to see what browsers do for _non_-early `Link` headers. Do they use `Content-Type`, or do they always use UTF-8?\r\n\r\nI hope that at least some browsers always use UTF-8, and so we can have the simple rule \"if it's a `Link` header, we use UTF-8; if it's `<link>`, we use the document's encoding\".",
